+# [MP8] Idempotency guard for hosting/joining (2026-08-17)
+#
+# Background. While the 8-player test rig ran Spine Breaker, `HOST button pressed` showed up **twice** in P1's log —
+# auto HOST only calls it once (the arguments.has("host") path), so the second one must have come from the UI button.
+# The test rig always needs a click on the window first to get focus (pitfall #19 - GameManager.game_focused starts as false),
+# and the HOST button sits right in that area, so **clicking the window for focus can easily hit it by accident**.
+#
+# The result isn't "an extra click is harmless". start_host() rebuilds the ENet server and resets player_order_by_seat
+# entirely. Peers that had already connected are lost, and later JOINs can't get in either —
+# on screen it looks like "P1 doesn't seem to have hosted, the other 7 are all stuck loading", which is hard to trace back to a misclick.
+#
+# ⚠️⚠️ The check must use **NetworkManager.active_backend**. Don't touch the SceneTree's multiplayer.
+#
+#   The first version used `multiplayer.has_multiplayer_peer()` + `get_connection_status()`,
+#   and it **blocked the auto HOST itself** (the log showed Auto HOST (P1) → immediately followed by "already online, ignoring").
+#   The root cause is that Godot 4 attaches an **OfflineMultiplayerPeer** to the SceneTree by default.
+#   `has_multiplayer_peer()` is always true and `get_connection_status()` is always CONNECTED
+#   (the offline peer considers itself the "connected" node with id=1). So that check is always true.
+#
+#   `active_backend` is this project's own field. It starts as null, only set_active_backend() inside create_backend()
+#   assigns it, and reset()/disconnect sets it back to null — so it means exactly "has hosted/connected or not".
+#   Also, in the Enet branch set_active_backend() runs synchronously (no await),
+#   so by the time a second misclick comes in it's already non-null and the guard holds.
+func _mp8_net_busy() -> bool :
+
+	return NetworkManager.active_backend != null
+
+
 func _on_host_button_pressed():
+	if _mp8_net_busy():
+		# Print the backend so if this ever wrongly blocks auto HOST again, the log shows directly what's holding it
+		print("[MP8] HOST pressed, but a backend already exists (%s) — ignoring (prevents a misclick from rebuilding the server)" % str(NetworkManager.active_backend))
+		return
+	print("[MP8] HOST button pressed")
 	NetworkManager.start_host(debug_lobby_handler.name_entry.text)
 
-	player_order_by_seat = {0: 1, 1: -1, 2: -1, 3: -1}
+	player_order_by_seat = {0: 1, 1: -1, 2: -1, 3: -1, 4: -1, 5: -1, 6: -1, 7: -1}  # [MP8]
